WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.410
In the beginning… there was a square.

2
00:00:03.410 --> 00:00:07.750
One hundred and twenty units. No more. No less.

3
00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:11.880
The logo demanded letters that obey the grid. Absolutely.

4
00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:23.050
It was born in the terminal. One module: half a character cell. One letter: four cells wide. If it doesn’t render in a terminal… it doesn’t exist.

5
00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:26.940
So we did not draw twenty-six letters. We drew six.

6
00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:30.840
O. P. E. N. C. D.

7
00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:36.120
The wordmark only ever needed six. Every other letter… was a compromise.

8
00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:39.290
No curves. Curves are indecision.

9
00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:41.740
No diagonals. No shortcuts.

10
00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:45.660
Every edge on the grid. Every corner on a whole module.

11
00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:51.670
Symmetry: measured. Ink coverage: counted. The shade: calibrated to the module.

12
00:00:51.670 --> 00:00:55.500
The o carries fourteen modules of ink. Exactly half.

13
00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:59.340
Thirty-six kerning pairs. Every value… zero.

14
00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:03.110
Not because we didn’t care. Because we cared… completely.

15
00:01:03.130 --> 00:01:06.970
Forty-nine kilobytes. Not one byte of decoration.

16
00:01:06.970 --> 00:01:12.170
Some typefaces have thousands of glyphs. This one has the only six that matter.

17
00:01:12.370 --> 00:01:24.630
Only six letters. Yet every visit maps the other 3,591 characters afresh. A number of combinations 2,795 digits long.

18
00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:28.130
Download it… and the typeface is yours alone.
